  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "class_subclasses",
    "file": "mruby/mrbgems/mruby-class-ext/src/class.c",
    "description": "`class_subclasses` calls `mrb_objspace_each_objects` to iterate all objects and pushes matching classes into a Ruby array. During this iteration, user-defined behavior is invoked indirectly (array/hash operations and object `hash` methods in the trace), and a full GC can run (`mrb_full_gc`), freeing string storage. The object-space iteration does not adequately protect against GC-sensitive side effects/reentrancy, so stale references are later consumed, leading to a heap-use-after-free when `mrb_str_hash` reads freed string bytes.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires executing `Class#subclasses` (from mruby-class-ext) in a script that, during the object-space walk, causes allocations/callbacks that run Ruby code and trigger GC (seen via hash insertion and `hash` dispatch). The fuzz input drives parser+VM to run such code; then GC frees a string buffer, and later hash key processing (`obj_hash_code` -> `mrb_str_hash`) reads the freed pointer, causing UAF."
  },
